  "verdict": "toa_separable_but_less_than_sr",
  "interpretation": "toa_not_separable: the land atmospheric correction (LaSRC in HLS) introduces the Landsat/Sentinel-2 difference over water. toa_as_separable: the difference is already present at top of atmosphere and arises from sensor calibration, spectral response and the acquisition-time difference. toa_separable_but_less_than_sr: most of the separability already exists at TOA; the atmospheric correction adds (does not remove) a smaller part. The HLS MSI->OLI bandpass coefficients were derived for surface reflectance; applied to TOA they move S2 blue away from OLI TOA and raise separability, so toa_bandpass is reported only as a check. Caveat: TOA includes path radiance (Rayleigh + aerosol, most of the TOA signal over water in the blue-green) that differs between the two acquisitions (solar/view geometry, aerosol change between overpasses), so TOA separability is not a pure sensor effect; the classifier can also use this geometry-driven path-radiance difference.",
